    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the point about reconstruction, but doesn't it seem like the main reason people call it a failure is because they're judging it based on humanitarian ideals? like, if we don't look at it through the lens of \"making things more democratic or stable,\" isn't there a real argument that toppling a dictator who was actively killing his own people is always a win for global security and human rights?",
